<ServiceLayout
  title="Chiropractic Social Media Marketing: Scope and Responsibilities | ChiroCandy"
  description="Compare ChiroCandy's social media scope, practice inputs, approvals, publishing, paid and organic boundaries, and reporting before choosing a service."
  slug="chiropractic-social-media-marketing"
  dateModified="2026-10-29"
  includeFaqSchema={false}
  heroTitle="Chiropractic Social Media Marketing: What Is Included?"
  heroAnswer="ChiroCandy offers social media content support for chiropractic practices. The current proposal should define the platforms, content types, cadence, approvals, publishing access, community response, reporting, and work your practice must supply; organic posting, paid advertising, and appointment outcomes are separate scopes and evidence sets."
  serviceName="Chiropractic Social Media Marketing"
  faqs={[
    {
      question: 'Which platforms and posting frequency are included?',
      answer:
        'Use the current ChiroCandy proposal as the source of truth. It should name each profile, content type, planned cadence, start date, and any volume or platform that is outside scope. This page does not promise a universal daily schedule or the same platform mix for every practice.',
    },
    {
      question: 'Does ChiroCandy create custom photos or video?',
      answer:
        'Confirm filming, photography, editing, captions, graphics, and revision limits in the current scope. When content depends on your office or team, the practice should name who supplies approved footage, accurate details, and permissions, plus the fallback when an asset is late.',
    },
    {
      question: 'Who approves posts and handles comments or direct messages?',
      answer:
        'The written workflow should name a practice approver, approval deadline, missed-deadline fallback, publishing owner, and the person responsible for comments and messages. Do not assume community moderation or lead response is included unless the agreement says so.',
    },
    {
      question: 'Are Facebook and Instagram ads included?',
      answer:
        'Organic social content and paid Meta advertising are separate workstreams. If both are purchased, the proposal should identify the advertising account, media budget, campaign management, creative reuse, lead destination, and reporting for each scope.',
    },
    {
      question: 'How should organic social results be measured?',
      answer:
        'Review platform delivery and engagement, profile activity, and tagged link traffic with their source and date window. Keep paid results, inquiries, booked appointments, held appointments, patients, and revenue separate; connect them only when the practice has an agreed definition and supporting record.',
